<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">Using the button and the pad</h2>
  <h3>The pad moves, the button acts.</h3>
  <p class="lede">
    skyBlip Go has two contacts worth learning: a capacitive pad on the top edge
    and a button on the side. The pad moves you around: a tap is the next page, a
    touch of a second brings the radar back. The button is the one that changes
    something: a press opens the settings and steps the row you are on, two quick
    presses authorise what the device is asking about, and a hold of two seconds
    switches it off.
  </p>
  <p>
    That split is the whole vocabulary, and it holds on every page: nothing a
    sleeve brushes against can change a setting, and nothing you do to walk the
    pages can be spent answering a question. The case carries one more input, a
    small <span class="mono">RST</span> button, which is the processor&rsquo;s
    reset and the way into the USB bootloader. It is covered at the foot of this
    page.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Gesture</th>
          <th>What it does</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th>Tap the pad</th>
          <td>next page; in the settings, moves the focus down a row</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Touch the pad, 1&nbsp;s</th>
          <td>back to the radar, from any page</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>One press of the button</th>
          <td>opens the settings; inside, acts on the focused row &mdash; or, at a question on the glass, refuses it</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Two presses, under 0.6&nbsp;s apart</th>
          <td>allows the question on the glass</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Hold the button, 2&nbsp;s</th>
          <td>switches the device off</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>The same hold, finger on the pad</th>
          <td>switches it off and leaves the screen blank, for storage</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

